course: dictionary
lesson: 10982
title: One word, three meanings: warmly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Warmly is a good example. It can mean keeping you warm, being kind and friendly, or showing strong feeling. «Wrap up warmly before you go out in the snow» is about clothes.
explain: «She smiled warmly at the new girl» is about kindness, not heat. Nobody's body gets hotter from a smile. Ask yourself: does this sentence talk about temperature, feelings, or enthusiasm? The clues around the word will tell you.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of warmly. If «She smiled kindly at the new girl» still makes sense, kindly is the right meaning.
fact: Warmly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: Warmly can mean in a way that keeps you warm: dress warmly, wrap up warmly.
fact: Warmly can mean in a kind, friendly, loving way: smile warmly, greet warmly, thank warmly.
fact: Warmly can mean strongly and with feeling: «the plan was warmly welcomed».
fact: Warmly has more forms: warmer, more warmly, and most warmly.
exercise: «When it snows, wrap up warmly before you go outside.» What does warmly mean here? | *In a way that keeps you warm | In a cold, unfriendly way | Loudly | Very quickly
exercise: «She smiled warmly at the new girl in class.» What does warmly show? | Anger | *A kind, friendly feeling | Tiredness | Confusion
exercise: «The plan was warmly welcomed by everyone at the meeting.» What does warmly suggest? | By just one person | *With strong feeling and enthusiasm | Quietly and secretly | With no feeling at all
test: «You can thank someone warmly for their thought and effort even when you do not like the gift.» Why should you thank the giver warmly? | Because you want a new gift | *Because the giver thought of you | Because you want to shout | Because the gift is too big to carry
test: Which sentence uses warmly to mean keeps you warm? | Greet them warmly when they arrive. | Thank him warmly for the card. | Smile warmly at the teacher. | *Dress warmly, with a hat, gloves and a scarf.
exam: A new classmate arrives on the first day. How should you greet them to make them feel welcome? | *Welcome them warmly with a smile | Turn your back and walk away | Ignore them and keep reading | Shout across the room at them
